          }
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "english_text": "Worse than that was killing Anbanandar, burying him in the palace garden, and falsely accusing him of having run away with the queen!... Look—here is Anbanandar's skeleton. I was the one who buried that holy man.",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "`அபாண்டம் சுமத்தியது` is rendered as laying a false accusation; the source's reverential `புனித மூர்த்தி` is kept as `holy man`."
        ]
      }
